# AI/ML Engineering

- Use ML only after defining the decision, target, prediction time, error costs, and deterministic baseline.
- Prevent leakage with point-in-time correct features and time-based dataset splits.
- Version source snapshots, labels, features, code, parameters, and model artifacts.
- Evaluate against simple and current-production baselines.
- Report performance by time period, vendor, store, category, and other relevant segments.
- Match metrics to business costs; accuracy alone is not sufficient.
- Measure uncertainty and calibration when scores trigger business actions.
- Require human approval for pricing, ad spend, catalog removal, and high-impact supplier actions.
- Monitor data freshness, feature drift, prediction drift, and realized outcomes.
- Provide a tested rollback path and deterministic fallback.
- Do not train on customer PII without documented purpose, approval, retention, and access controls.
- Never claim causation from observational correlations or temporal coincidence.
